Would it make sense to include `AsWorkflow` in this change too, allowing it to be extended and ensuring derived attributes are recognized by autoconfiguration/discovery?

Our use case is to build a smaller workflow-extras bundle on top of the native attributes, while leaving workflow definition and registration entirely to Symfony. If all three attributes are extensible, we can add convenience arguments such as `description:` to our subclasses and map them to ordinary workflow, place and transition metadata.

We've found these options useful in our tooling, but recognize that some bundle-specific options don't belong in core. Extensibility would let us keep those in our own subclasses and experiment with them without needing a core argument for every enhancement. A workflow-level description used by our explorer and documentation is one simple example; I also opened #66726 to discuss whether descriptions themselves would be useful in core.

